I. Introduction

The proliferation of road accidents necessitates exploration of innovative solutions to bolster rider safety. While traditional helmets offer essential head protection, they lack functionalities to address scenarios beyond physical impact as shown in fig 1. This research investigates the potential of smart helmets, which integrate various sensors and technologies, to enhance situational awareness, provide real-time assistance, and expedite emergency response in the event of accidents [6], [7], [10]–[13].
